> In Julia, to check if each element in vector `A` is contained in vector `B` individually, you can use broadcasting with the `in` function. The syntax `in.(A, Ref(B))` ensures that each element of `A` is checked for membership in `B`. Here's how you can do it:
> 
> ```julia
> A = [1, 2, 3]
> B = [2, 3, 4, 5]
> 
> result = in.(A, Ref(B))
> println(result)  # Output: [false, true, true]
> ```
> 
> This will return a boolean array where each element corresponds to whether the element in `A` is found in `B`. The use of `Ref(B)` ensures that the entire vector `B` is treated as a single argument for the `in` function during the broadcasting operation.
